# Copy to .env if you want to enable a cloud AI provider. All optional.
# With every value absent, the backend runs in rules/template mode
# (ai_status=unavailable) and /explain still returns template explanations.
# Never commit a real key.
#
# AI_PROVIDER: openai | deepseek | gemini
# AI_MODEL: e.g. gpt-4o-mini | deepseek-chat | gemini-2.0-flash
#   Third-party OpenAI-compatible gateways: set AI_PROVIDER=deepseek (or
#   openai) and AI_BASE_URL to the gateway base URL. Working gateway
#   (2026-11-25, tested live): shenjyai.cc — AI_BASE_URL=
#   https://www.shenjyai.cc/v1 with AI_MODEL=deepseek-v4.1-flash.
#   Do NOT use ai11.shop: its key was rejected with "Invalid token".
# AI_API_KEY: the provider key. The user supplies it (Secure Vault);
#   the agent never buys, stores or commits one.
# AI_BASE_URL: optional override (default per provider, see ai/provider.py).
# AI_TIMEOUT_MS: total call budget in ms (default 20000, spec Ch13/Ch17).
# AI_MAX_TOKENS: max output tokens per call (default 1200).
AI_PROVIDER=
AI_MODEL=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_BASE_URL=
AI_TIMEOUT_MS=
AI_MAX_TOKENS=
